# Local configuration overlay

Drop only the `config/*.py` files you actually override in here. At startup the MCRIT containers
copy `config/` into the installed package's config directory and then copy whatever is in this
directory on top, so a file here replaces the shipped default of the same name and everything else
keeps tracking the repository.

Everything in this directory except this README is gitignored, so a deployment's own settings - an
`McritConfig.py` carrying an `AUTH_TOKEN`, a `StorageConfig.py` pointing at an external MongoDB -
survive a `git pull` and never reach a commit.

A file here is a whole module: copy the shipped `config/<name>.py`, edit it, and keep the rest of
its settings, or the startup drift check will report the ones you dropped.
